1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,619
On the morning of December 7th, 1941, the United States was still a country at peace.

2
00:00:06,619 --> 00:00:08,339
By nightfall it was not.

3
00:00:08,339 --> 00:00:13,148
The first Japanese aircraft reached Pearl Harbor at 7:48 in the morning.

4
00:00:13,148 --> 00:00:15,541
The attack lasted 110 minutes.

5
00:00:15,541 --> 00:00:24,922
When it ended, eight battleships had been sunk or damaged, 188 aircraft were destroyed, and 2,403 Americans were dead.

6
00:00:24,922 --> 00:00:29,212
Franklin Roosevelt spent that evening dictating a message to Congress.

7
00:00:29,212 --> 00:00:40,561
In the draft he crossed out the words "a date which will live in world history" and wrote instead: "a date which will live in infamy." The next afternoon the Senate voted for war, 82 votes to nothing.

8
00:00:40,561 --> 00:00:43,430
The House agreed, 388 to 1.

9
00:00:43,430 --> 00:00:47,480
What followed was an industrial mobilization without precedent.

10
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:52,295
In 1941 American shipyards launched fewer than 100 merchant vessels.

11
00:00:52,295 --> 00:00:56,563
By 1943 they were launching more than 1,900 a year.

